{
 "voice": "archive (bm_fable 0.40 + am_michael 0.40 + bm_lewis 0.20)",
 "style_md5": "c9ce4988",
 "speed": 0.92,
 "question_speed": 0.8522,
 "duration": 835.994,
 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "Right now, about thirty miles from the White House, more than a hundred ships are rotting in the Potomac River.",
   "start": 0.35,
   "end": 6.54,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 0,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "807be7bfd891.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Not one or two.",
   "start": 7.14,
   "end": 8.368,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 1,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "76ce869752c9.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A whole fleet.",
   "start": 8.668,
   "end": 9.825,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 1,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b0ef114adb6e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "America built them to win the First World War.",
   "start": 10.425,
   "end": 13.357,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 2,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ccb669392a93.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Each one cost more than seven hundred and fifty thousand dollars.",
   "start": 13.657,
   "end": 17.389,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 2,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9d76a694e568.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Most were finished after the war was already over.",
   "start": 17.689,
   "end": 20.694,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 2,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "2b56b0fe5cc2.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "So the government sold them.",
   "start": 21.294,
   "end": 22.861,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 3,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ea99d8009449.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "For about three thousand dollars each.",
   "start": 23.161,
   "end": 25.303,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 3,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "190b6482dce3.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the buyers set them on fire.",
   "start": 25.603,
   "end": 27.598,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 3,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b31031077e86.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Thirty-one ships went up in flames at once.",
   "start": 27.898,
   "end": 30.396,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 3,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "40972e2857b7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And still, they would not go away.",
   "start": 30.996,
   "end": 32.964,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 4,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "06c5fe05772a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A steel giant tried to break them up.",
   "start": 33.264,
   "end": 35.443,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 4,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8b03756ad949.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Congress ordered them removed.",
   "start": 35.743,
   "end": 37.664,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 4,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e68c514b2975.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Everything failed.",
   "start": 37.964,
   "end": 39.136,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 4,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0abe067f906b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Today, trees grow out of their hulls.",
   "start": 39.736,
   "end": 41.9,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 5,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "fba51faf7d9a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ospreys nest on their timbers.",
   "start": 42.2,
   "end": 44.091,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 5,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "168e454b3163.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "So why is the fleet still here?",
   "start": 44.691,
   "end": 46.729,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 6,
   "speed": 0.8522,
   "file": "3772e600e8e7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The answer is not what anyone in Washington planned.",
   "start": 47.029,
   "end": 50.279,
   "chapter": "c01",
   "para": 6,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3dac21004ced.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Start with what you would see from the air.",
   "start": 51.179,
   "end": 53.405,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 7,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c80839462bb8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the Maryland shore of the Potomac, in Charles County, near a place called Nanjemoy, there is a small bay.",
   "start": 53.705,
   "end": 60.188,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 7,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e0ff4735a964.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Mallows Bay.",
   "start": 60.488,
   "end": 61.537,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 7,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "2039bb7ec4ae.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At low tide, dark shapes rise out of the water.",
   "start": 62.137,
   "end": 65.117,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 8,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3bd98b0b0ffa.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Long ovals, all about the same size, lying side by side.",
   "start": 65.417,
   "end": 69.449,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 8,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4f6ffe45158b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Some are bare ribs.",
   "start": 69.749,
   "end": 71.046,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 8,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d4d922282779.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Some carry whole trees.",
   "start": 71.346,
   "end": 72.956,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 8,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8c24b426e188.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Each shape is the hull of a wooden steamship.",
   "start": 73.556,
   "end": 76.222,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 9,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f0053f697c3d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Federal surveys count more than a hundred of them from the First World War alone.",
   "start": 76.522,
   "end": 81.169,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 9,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d6289db13577.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "NOAA counts one hundred and forty-one known shipwrecks in and around the bay.",
   "start": 81.469,
   "end": 86.199,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 9,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b847f72ce075.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The bay is thirty-two miles from the White House, as the crow flies.",
   "start": 86.799,
   "end": 90.992,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 10,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "56aaf1876126.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Yet most people in Washington have never heard of it.",
   "start": 91.292,
   "end": 94.398,
   "chapter": "c02",
   "para": 10,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "56274a4f7af3.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "To understand how a fleet ended up here, go back to the spring of nineteen seventeen.",
   "start": 95.298,
   "end": 100.3,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 11,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "638a77a891c3.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In February and March of nineteen seventeen, German U-boats sank more than a million tons of shipping.",
   "start": 100.9,
   "end": 107.224,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 12,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "930b4caf72c9.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Britain was running out of ships faster than it could build them.",
   "start": 107.524,
   "end": 110.824,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 12,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "69fea0b720db.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the sixth of April, the United States declared war on Germany.",
   "start": 111.424,
   "end": 115.442,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 13,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "582b794e2747.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Now it had to send an army across the Atlantic.",
   "start": 115.742,
   "end": 118.623,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 13,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "28ebcce5b72f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And it did not have the ships to carry it.",
   "start": 118.923,
   "end": 121.023,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 13,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "599f310f7db5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ten days later, the government created the Emergency Fleet Corporation.",
   "start": 121.623,
   "end": 125.724,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 14,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "cfb01c31421d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Its job was to build ships faster than the U-boats could sink them.",
   "start": 126.024,
   "end": 129.922,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 14,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6ad099bf6ca6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Steel was short.",
   "start": 130.522,
   "end": 131.741,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 15,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "2aba3c7e9b97.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Shipyards were full.",
   "start": 132.041,
   "end": 133.392,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 15,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "123f645acec3.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "So someone proposed something that sounded almost old-fashioned.",
   "start": 133.692,
   "end": 137.54,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 15,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c4dc10510990.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Build the ships out of wood.",
   "start": 137.84,
   "end": 139.471,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 15,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b73730f22a62.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "America had forests, and it had carpenters.",
   "start": 140.071,
   "end": 142.792,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 16,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "50aced297a5f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The plan called for as many as a thousand wooden steamships in eighteen months.",
   "start": 143.092,
   "end": 147.903,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 16,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3b688e598624.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The standard design came from a naval architect named Theodore Ferris.",
   "start": 148.503,
   "end": 152.796,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 17,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "07478ebc9e40.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A wooden hull about two hundred and eighty-one feet long.",
   "start": 153.096,
   "end": 156.479,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 17,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a17647497152.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It carried about three thousand five hundred tons of cargo, and it burned coal.",
   "start": 156.779,
   "end": 161.527,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 17,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "533fc5e2b424.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Its top speed was about ten knots.",
   "start": 162.127,
   "end": 164.42,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 18,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6f4b053dbe9c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Slow, even then.",
   "start": 164.72,
   "end": 166.027,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 18,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ecc3cd2ca894.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But it could be built almost anywhere there was timber and water.",
   "start": 166.327,
   "end": 169.907,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 18,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b632b85738d9.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "By nineteen nineteen, the government counted eighty-seven yards building wooden ships.",
   "start": 170.507,
   "end": 175.61,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 19,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6ec54416192a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the Pacific coast, on the Gulf coast and along the Atlantic.",
   "start": 175.91,
   "end": 179.687,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 19,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7f1a7ae3e21e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At the peak, in September nineteen eighteen, more than eighty thousand people were building wooden ships.",
   "start": 180.287,
   "end": 186.103,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 20,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a148e0c4ba52.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The first one slid into the water in Oregon on the first of December, nineteen seventeen.",
   "start": 186.703,
   "end": 192.183,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 21,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e2405127613b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was called the North Bend.",
   "start": 192.483,
   "end": 194.184,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 21,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "26a6acc1b10f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Remember that name.",
   "start": 194.484,
   "end": 195.731,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 21,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "bedaa0cebe45.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In Aberdeen, Washington, a yard claimed a record.",
   "start": 196.331,
   "end": 199.641,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 22,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9dbf823387f1.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A hull built from keel to launch in seventeen and a half days.",
   "start": 199.941,
   "end": 203.54,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 22,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8403cd81f3dc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "They named her the Aberdeen.",
   "start": 203.84,
   "end": 205.555,
   "chapter": "c03",
   "para": 22,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5a8c662ad35c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On paper, it looked like a miracle.",
   "start": 206.455,
   "end": 208.597,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 23,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "31a20ef67742.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the water, it was something else.",
   "start": 208.897,
   "end": 210.891,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 23,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "df51183fa42a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The timber was often green.",
   "start": 211.491,
   "end": 213.218,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 24,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b5278a3a9fd7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Freshly cut wood shrinks as it dries, and the seams of the hulls opened.",
   "start": 213.518,
   "end": 217.95,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 24,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "54ede050ceae.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Many of the ships leaked.",
   "start": 218.25,
   "end": 219.864,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 24,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b5c8babe2298.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Wood is not as strong as steel, so a wooden hull could only be built so long.",
   "start": 220.464,
   "end": 225.054,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 25,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b9defba8caf7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The ships were small for ocean cargo, and they burned a lot of coal.",
   "start": 225.354,
   "end": 229.266,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 25,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a35aac77b3f6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The government's own shipping board said they were suited only for short trips.",
   "start": 229.566,
   "end": 233.852,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 25,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "23eb1b04e328.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And they were late.",
   "start": 234.452,
   "end": 235.599,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 26,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5b00961a9ad1.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "From August nineteen eighteen, the yards were finally delivering about one wooden ship a day.",
   "start": 235.899,
   "end": 241.434,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 26,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b1aca0be26a6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But by the end of October, only ninety-two wooden and composite ships had been delivered.",
   "start": 241.734,
   "end": 246.932,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 26,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0d8a25ea10fb.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, on the eleventh of November nineteen eighteen, the war ended.",
   "start": 247.532,
   "end": 251.596,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 27,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f0590d6dd4e0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "According to the government's own historic survey, not one of the wooden ships reached a port in Europe while the fighting lasted.",
   "start": 252.196,
   "end": 259.593,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 28,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "fc9c45dfded2.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But the yards kept building.",
   "start": 260.193,
   "end": 261.755,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 29,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "76dfbf42d1b4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Contracts had been signed.",
   "start": 262.055,
   "end": 263.749,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 29,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d84c1a91683b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Workers had to be paid.",
   "start": 264.049,
   "end": 265.823,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 29,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e73897bdec48.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Hundreds of hulls were already on the ways.",
   "start": 266.123,
   "end": 268.646,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 29,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "779345642b6e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the end, three hundred and twenty-two of them were finished.",
   "start": 269.246,
   "end": 272.401,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 30,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6f09de8bc94b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "About seven in ten were delivered after the war was already over.",
   "start": 272.701,
   "end": 276.695,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 30,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6e84289a478b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "By the middle of nineteen twenty, the shipping board had spent more than two hundred and seventy-four million dollars on wooden and composite ships.",
   "start": 277.295,
   "end": 285.758,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 31,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "040cce58d0d8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "For a short time after the war, they were put to work.",
   "start": 286.358,
   "end": 289.306,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 32,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0c04c8e48602.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In April nineteen twenty, as many as two hundred and forty of them were in service.",
   "start": 289.606,
   "end": 294.618,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 32,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "43b4f86b6a47.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Some of them did cross the Atlantic, carrying coal and cargo.",
   "start": 294.918,
   "end": 298.768,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 32,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c3074020f093.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then world shipping slumped.",
   "start": 299.368,
   "end": 301.085,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 33,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "76489aced6e2.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "There were suddenly too many ships, and nobody wanted slow, leaky wooden ones.",
   "start": 301.385,
   "end": 305.989,
   "chapter": "c04",
   "para": 33,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4b91d339913c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "So the government tried to sell them.",
   "start": 306.889,
   "end": 308.745,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 34,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f902c4d40020.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In nineteen nineteen and nineteen twenty, the board was getting about two hundred thousand dollars a ship.",
   "start": 309.045,
   "end": 315.331,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 34,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "71aa3e5b6826.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "By nineteen twenty-one, it sold twenty-one of them for about five thousand seven hundred dollars each.",
   "start": 315.931,
   "end": 321.904,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 35,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0fbb875b99a6.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The rest were tied up in long rows, waiting.",
   "start": 322.504,
   "end": 325.132,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 36,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3bfee8bcf143.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The biggest gathering was in the James River, in Virginia.",
   "start": 325.432,
   "end": 328.883,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 36,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7028077be278.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the twelfth of September nineteen twenty-two, the government gave up.",
   "start": 329.483,
   "end": 333.639,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 37,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "623292e9a58f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It auctioned off two hundred and thirty-three wooden steamships in a single lot.",
   "start": 333.939,
   "end": 338.615,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 37,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "74f4ec199da5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The price was seven hundred and fifty thousand dollars.",
   "start": 339.215,
   "end": 342.519,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 38,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c5a0099b6509.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "For all of them.",
   "start": 342.819,
   "end": 343.926,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 38,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d9a0df641a12.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "That is about three thousand two hundred dollars a ship.",
   "start": 344.226,
   "end": 347.281,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 38,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4d1dd21cdc1a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The buyer's company was called Western Marine and Salvage.",
   "start": 347.881,
   "end": 351.457,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 39,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a29d326cb8bc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And the deal came with one condition.",
   "start": 351.757,
   "end": 353.799,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 39,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8ced87dd9968.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The ships could never sail as steamers again.",
   "start": 354.099,
   "end": 356.545,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 39,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "1aab591c331f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "They had to be broken up.",
   "start": 356.845,
   "end": 358.471,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 39,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "bf20a8bb38bb.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The plan was simple.",
   "start": 359.071,
   "end": 360.456,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 40,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9661ead425da.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Strip out the engines, the boilers and everything metal.",
   "start": 360.756,
   "end": 363.962,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 40,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "60ee36241c79.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then burn the wooden hulls down to the waterline and collect what was left.",
   "start": 364.262,
   "end": 368.591,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 40,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b39154714867.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The company towed the ships up the Potomac.",
   "start": 369.191,
   "end": 371.639,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 41,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "fbf1780379c5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Some went to Alexandria, just across the river from Washington.",
   "start": 371.939,
   "end": 375.83,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 41,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ddc9e9f4de25.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Most were anchored off Widewater, Virginia, near the Marine base at Quantico.",
   "start": 376.13,
   "end": 380.958,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 41,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d25bfaf7e9f0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It went wrong almost at once.",
   "start": 381.558,
   "end": 383.393,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 42,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "962ea962c0c1.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In October nineteen twenty-two, a fire broke out on two of the ships at Alexandria, blamed on a cigarette.",
   "start": 383.693,
   "end": 390.757,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 42,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9d29e27197bc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In April nineteen twenty-three, fire broke out again, this time at Widewater.",
   "start": 391.357,
   "end": 396.297,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 43,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9ecf526e8b95.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Five ships were destroyed.",
   "start": 396.597,
   "end": 398.213,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 43,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "89fb806e4650.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "One of them was the Aberdeen, the record-breaker.",
   "start": 398.513,
   "end": 401.419,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 43,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "244dfe93aa3a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was raised, and later burned again, as a test.",
   "start": 401.719,
   "end": 404.727,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 43,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ae3912acc73b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The local watermen were furious.",
   "start": 405.327,
   "end": 407.308,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 44,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "18d87b3ae487.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Their shad and herring nets were in the same water.",
   "start": 407.608,
   "end": 410.512,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 44,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d3bee82c74bf.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sunken hulls and floating wreckage threatened their living.",
   "start": 410.812,
   "end": 414.261,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 44,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "28f8e7814187.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "They complained all the way to Washington.",
   "start": 414.561,
   "end": 416.965,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 44,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5b34db28b63a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "So the company looked for a place out of the way.",
   "start": 417.565,
   "end": 420.053,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 45,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8961da2af87d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In April nineteen twenty-four, it bought land on the Maryland side, across from Widewater.",
   "start": 420.353,
   "end": 426.145,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 45,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "bcb53665414a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Around a quiet bay.",
   "start": 426.445,
   "end": 427.794,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 45,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "fae6e751d1c4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Mallows Bay.",
   "start": 428.394,
   "end": 429.444,
   "chapter": "c05",
   "para": 46,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "2039bb7ec4ae.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the seventh of November nineteen twenty-five, the company tried to finish the job in one go.",
   "start": 430.344,
   "end": 436.194,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 47,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "492ad09d7397.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At five in the morning, thirty-one ships were set on fire at once.",
   "start": 436.794,
   "end": 440.514,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 48,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b4384b97801f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Across the river, at the Marine base at Quantico, sentries saw the glow.",
   "start": 441.114,
   "end": 445.501,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 49,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "534527dee7c0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The newspaper said it looked like the red ball of the sun.",
   "start": 445.801,
   "end": 448.896,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 49,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4923747f7b25.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A Marine Corps plane flew over and photographed the blaze.",
   "start": 449.196,
   "end": 452.551,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 49,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d7b84b522e59.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Above the flames, the paper said, the plane was nearly flipped over.",
   "start": 452.851,
   "end": 456.969,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 49,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "ea9dfb1401de.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "One reporter wrote that as the decks burned, rats poured off the ships.",
   "start": 457.569,
   "end": 461.843,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 50,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8ea7e4dce8d3.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "When it was over, the company had what it came for.",
   "start": 462.443,
   "end": 465.163,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 51,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "44543a89bdb4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A little iron and steel, pulled from the ashes.",
   "start": 465.463,
   "end": 468.293,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 51,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "276d7512203e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "After that, the company gave up on burning ships in big batches.",
   "start": 468.893,
   "end": 472.58,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 52,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "de49c42f73e9.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It burned them one at a time.",
   "start": 472.88,
   "end": 474.644,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 52,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "85555fe3f34f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Over the next years, the burned hulls were packed into Mallows Bay.",
   "start": 475.244,
   "end": 478.844,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 53,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "36580855f70a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In all, the company said, it brought one hundred and sixty-nine ships here.",
   "start": 479.144,
   "end": 483.566,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 53,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "2aaca2b360b7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It never made the money it hoped for.",
   "start": 484.166,
   "end": 486.087,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 54,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "99f232b66eb7.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then came the Great Depression.",
   "start": 486.387,
   "end": 488.23,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 54,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "93e1936c04f2.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In nineteen thirty-one, the company stopped work.",
   "start": 488.53,
   "end": 491.55,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 54,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "35957e75531a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "By the end of nineteen thirty-two, it had been dissolved.",
   "start": 491.85,
   "end": 495.229,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 54,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5f60ff6f99cb.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The ships were still there.",
   "start": 495.829,
   "end": 497.297,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 55,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "2d87dc28b74f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Now local people moved in.",
   "start": 497.897,
   "end": 499.694,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 56,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "cd58ed10c70e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the hungry years of the Depression, families rowed out to the wrecks and pried out bolts, spikes and iron, and sold them as scrap.",
   "start": 499.994,
   "end": 507.735,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 56,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0720ec5c3f14.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The fight over the scrap ended up in court.",
   "start": 508.335,
   "end": 510.788,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 57,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "38753eb7692a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In January nineteen thirty-six, Maryland's highest court ruled that the wrecks had been abandoned.",
   "start": 511.088,
   "end": 517.057,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 57,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8d92d009ab0a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Anyone could take what was left.",
   "start": 517.357,
   "end": 519.361,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 57,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "24f0beba14d4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "That April, an Army camera plane flew over the bay.",
   "start": 519.961,
   "end": 522.956,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 58,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e3a72458d611.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It caught the fleet lying in rows, hull against hull.",
   "start": 523.256,
   "end": 526.367,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 58,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5ced30b45a79.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "There is an old story that the wrecks hid floating brothels and whiskey stills in those years.",
   "start": 526.967,
   "end": 532.293,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 59,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c58e2745567b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It is a good story.",
   "start": 532.593,
   "end": 533.961,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 59,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "dc16645d6cfc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But the historian who wrote the official survey found no evidence for it.",
   "start": 534.261,
   "end": 538.51,
   "chapter": "c06",
   "para": 59,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "bfacaa107d98.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, in nineteen forty-one, America went to war again.",
   "start": 539.41,
   "end": 542.95,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 60,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "945e0ef2ff9d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And this time, the wrecks seemed to have one more job to do.",
   "start": 543.25,
   "end": 546.449,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 60,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c5d18c8ad6d0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The new war needed steel.",
   "start": 547.049,
   "end": 548.601,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 61,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "56e17e021276.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Every scrap drive in the country was collecting pots, pans and old cars.",
   "start": 548.901,
   "end": 553.692,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 61,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "bd7e0068034f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And in Mallows Bay, there were thousands of tons of iron sitting in the mud.",
   "start": 553.992,
   "end": 558.119,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 61,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "55899a15700c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In nineteen forty-two, the government hired one of the biggest steel companies in the country.",
   "start": 558.719,
   "end": 564.115,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 62,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "482360072ba8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Bethlehem Steel.",
   "start": 564.415,
   "end": 565.607,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 62,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "7f29c4205ef2.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The plan was clever.",
   "start": 566.207,
   "end": 567.589,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 63,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "26e83d1a43c1.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Bethlehem built a basin at the edge of the bay, with dams and gates.",
   "start": 567.889,
   "end": 571.971,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 63,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a484a896b7fa.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Hulls would be floated in, the water pumped out, and the wood burned away on dry ground.",
   "start": 572.271,
   "end": 577.646,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 63,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4d5c01350a1d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The target was up to twenty thousand tons of scrap metal.",
   "start": 578.246,
   "end": 581.754,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 64,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5dc2f680653a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It did not work.",
   "start": 582.354,
   "end": 583.541,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 65,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "78d04a3541c9.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "According to the records, by the end of nineteen forty-three Bethlehem had spent three hundred and sixty thousand dollars.",
   "start": 583.841,
   "end": 590.827,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 65,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e0cdda6c83a2.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And the result was, quote, a very small recovery of metal.",
   "start": 591.127,
   "end": 594.712,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 65,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f395cd170637.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In September nineteen forty-four, the government ended the contract.",
   "start": 595.312,
   "end": 599.604,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 66,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9816c2ef9af5.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The fleet that missed one world war had now missed a second.",
   "start": 599.904,
   "end": 603.485,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 66,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f1b983b7f489.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The basin is still there.",
   "start": 604.085,
   "end": 605.642,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 67,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f236254bf29c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "You can still see its outline from the air, at the mouth of a creek at the edge of the bay.",
   "start": 605.942,
   "end": 610.979,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 67,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "602d077c4f61.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "After the war, the wrecks were mostly forgotten.",
   "start": 611.579,
   "end": 614.295,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 68,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "dd0ffdfcf820.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, in October nineteen sixty-three, a company called Idamont bought the farm on Sandy Point, right beside the bay.",
   "start": 614.595,
   "end": 622.308,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 68,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6720b0862d18.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Army Corps of Engineers offered a cheap fix.",
   "start": 622.908,
   "end": 625.799,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 69,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "78efe4ecf4ad.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Pin the outer wrecks in place with stone, for about fifty thousand dollars.",
   "start": 626.099,
   "end": 630.607,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 69,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c4689a62242b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The landowner said no.",
   "start": 630.907,
   "end": 632.349,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 69,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0bf4afec1f6c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It wanted the wrecks gone.",
   "start": 632.649,
   "end": 634.083,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 69,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d52bd649d3c8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In nineteen sixty-eight, Congress ordered the wrecks removed, at an estimated three hundred and fifty thousand dollars, if Maryland paid half.",
   "start": 634.683,
   "end": 643.381,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 70,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "bfa4e634ea04.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Maryland would not pay.",
   "start": 643.681,
   "end": 645.322,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 70,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0be486fba08f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And here is the twist.",
   "start": 645.922,
   "end": 647.409,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 71,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "262e91a6ee4b.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In nineteen seventy, at a hearing in Congress, a vice-president of the power company PEPCO was asked about Idamont.",
   "start": 647.709,
   "end": 655.306,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 71,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6e983590f4bc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Under oath, he called it a dummy corporation, formed by PEPCO.",
   "start": 655.606,
   "end": 659.561,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 71,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d684cf1d77a4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The power company had been quietly buying the land beside the fleet for a new power plant.",
   "start": 660.161,
   "end": 665.087,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 72,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f12845f9f112.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "It denied any part in the push to remove the wrecks.",
   "start": 665.387,
   "end": 668.509,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 72,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "5a00d5ee5576.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But the wrecks were right in front of its land.",
   "start": 668.809,
   "end": 671.065,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 72,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "68daf63ba7fb.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "That same year, the Army counted ninety-nine hulks still in Mallows Bay.",
   "start": 671.665,
   "end": 675.897,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 73,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b2d0b1a739f1.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And Maryland's natural resources department said clearing them would serve no public interest.",
   "start": 676.197,
   "end": 682.159,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 73,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "03df25da30f4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Because while everyone had been arguing about the ships, something else had moved in.",
   "start": 682.759,
   "end": 687.315,
   "chapter": "c07",
   "para": 74,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "34dd692779a0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "To answer the question, go back out on the water.",
   "start": 688.215,
   "end": 691.109,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 75,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4a4622c50035.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "When the hulls were burned, their bottoms were left in the mud, packed with dirt and ash.",
   "start": 691.709,
   "end": 696.466,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 76,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d07017e8689e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Over the years, river silt filled them up.",
   "start": 696.766,
   "end": 699.24,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 76,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "eebb389d23fc.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Seeds blew in.",
   "start": 699.84,
   "end": 700.977,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 77,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4537f7fc0633.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then bushes.",
   "start": 701.277,
   "end": 702.284,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 77,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c206653c2880.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then trees.",
   "start": 702.584,
   "end": 703.645,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 77,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f2590150fb60.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "By nineteen seventy, whole trees were growing out of the hulks, like plants in giant flowerpots.",
   "start": 703.945,
   "end": 710.086,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 77,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "b29495ce49df.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The wrecks had become islands.",
   "start": 710.686,
   "end": 712.574,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 78,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a26f4fd00787.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ship-shaped islands, with their own trees.",
   "start": 712.874,
   "end": 715.376,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 78,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "45392f824769.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Fish moved into the ribs.",
   "start": 715.976,
   "end": 717.72,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 79,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3717653af260.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Largemouth bass, striped bass, shad, herring.",
   "start": 718.02,
   "end": 721.025,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 79,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "3229381eda71.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ospreys built nests on the high timbers.",
   "start": 721.625,
   "end": 724.103,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 80,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4f0b964d169c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Bald eagles hunt over the bay.",
   "start": 724.403,
   "end": 726.357,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 80,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "d9239c90bd2e.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "On one wreck, surveyors found a beaver lodge built inside the hull.",
   "start": 726.957,
   "end": 730.853,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 81,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a25f81a3cbda.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The beavers had chewed an exit hole right through the side of the ship.",
   "start": 731.153,
   "end": 734.998,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 81,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a38f0637f30a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Not every wreck here is from the First World War.",
   "start": 735.598,
   "end": 738.306,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 82,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "23553038f0b4.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "At the edge of the bay lies a steel car ferry, the Accomac.",
   "start": 738.606,
   "end": 742.023,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 82,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "4fd34f6ee1f2.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was built in nineteen twenty-eight, burned in nineteen sixty-four, and was towed here years later.",
   "start": 742.323,
   "end": 748.227,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 82,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "1f5c9aea6c8d.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ospreys have been nesting on her since at least nineteen eighty-six.",
   "start": 748.827,
   "end": 752.838,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 83,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e55d2c04bc9f.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And somewhere in the bay lies the North Bend.",
   "start": 753.438,
   "end": 755.999,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 84,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a3ddd1115873.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The very first wooden ship of the program.",
   "start": 756.299,
   "end": 758.819,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 84,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e06929cf736c.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The ship that started it all ended up here too.",
   "start": 759.119,
   "end": 761.845,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 84,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "34073af429b0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "In April twenty fifteen, the wrecks were listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
   "start": 762.445,
   "end": 767.98,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 85,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "1984dbb4b655.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And in September twenty nineteen, the bay and the river around it became the Mallows Bay-Potomac River National Marine Sanctuary.",
   "start": 768.58,
   "end": 776.66,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 86,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "00f02f62251a.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Eighteen square miles.",
   "start": 776.96,
   "end": 778.431,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 86,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "9754b588f1a0.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The first new national marine sanctuary in nearly twenty years.",
   "start": 778.731,
   "end": 782.813,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 86,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "65b78f8e4712.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "NOAA calls it the largest wooden ship graveyard in the Western Hemisphere.",
   "start": 783.413,
   "end": 787.947,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 87,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "a48a5747de84.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Today you can paddle a kayak through the fleet, right over the ribs of ships built to fight the Kaiser.",
   "start": 788.247,
   "end": 794.1,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 87,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "25894c3fab96.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "So that is the answer.",
   "start": 794.7,
   "end": 796.281,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 88,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e16af6249696.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The fleet is still here because every attempt to get rid of it failed.",
   "start": 796.581,
   "end": 800.535,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 88,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "0e4ae1f8e651.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "And while those attempts failed, the river turned the fleet into something nobody planned.",
   "start": 800.835,
   "end": 805.735,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 88,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "c787bdea86ec.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "A habitat.",
   "start": 806.035,
   "end": 806.98,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 88,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "1abeb9df58d8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "The same government that paid a fortune to build these ships, and then sold them off to be destroyed, now protects them by law.",
   "start": 807.58,
   "end": 814.898,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 89,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "32b99242fbcf.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "But the fleet will not last forever.",
   "start": 815.498,
   "end": 817.539,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 90,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "6d4da1914524.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "About seven in ten of the wrecks that could be seen in nineteen ninety-eight now sit just under the surface, even at low tide.",
   "start": 817.839,
   "end": 825.488,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 90,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "f4c77a7f0583.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "So here is the question.",
   "start": 826.088,
   "end": 827.677,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 91,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "8842cbc824e8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Should we try to save what is left of it?",
   "start": 827.977,
   "end": 830.178,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 91,
   "speed": 0.8522,
   "file": "147e749b2ac8.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Or let the river finish the job?",
   "start": 830.478,
   "end": 832.565,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 91,
   "speed": 0.8522,
   "file": "09a1d0a534e1.wav"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tell us what you think in the comments.",
   "start": 832.865,
   "end": 834.994,
   "chapter": "c08",
   "para": 91,
   "speed": 0.92,
   "file": "e55f38a729be.wav"
  }
 ]
}